   $q$A boat travels 36 kilometers downstream in 2 hours and returns the same 36 kilometers upstream in 3 hours. The current speeds the boat up going downstream and slows it down going upstream by the same amount. What is the speed of the current, in kilometers per hour?$q$, $q$[{"text":"15","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-other-unknown"},{"text":"3","is_correct":true},{"text":"6","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-halve-difference"},{"text":"18","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-downstream-speed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$3$q$, $q$Downstream speed is $36 \div 2 = 18$ and upstream speed is $36 \div 3 = 12$. With boat speed $b$ and current $c$: $b + c = 18$ and $b - c = 12$. Subtracting gives $2c = 6$, so $c = 3$. The value 15 is the boat's speed in still water, and 6 is $2c$ before dividing by $2$.$q$, 'draft', null)
