  ('90373938-1506-5496-84e5-299cabfb9535', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'systems-linear'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Gym P charges 50 dollars to join plus 25 dollars per month. Gym Q charges 20 dollars to join plus 35 dollars per month. Which statement is true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The total costs are equal after 3 months and stay equal every month after that.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-lines-coincide"},{"text":"The total costs are equal after 3 months, and Gym Q costs less for a full year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-after-intersection"},{"text":"The total costs are equal after 7 months, and Gym P costs less for a full year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-flat-fees"},{"text":"The total costs are equal after 3 months, and Gym P costs less for a full year.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The total costs are equal after 3 months, and Gym P costs less for a full year.$q$, $q$Set the totals equal: $50 + 25m = 20 + 35m$, so $30 = 10m$ and $m = 3$. For 12 months, Gym P costs $50 + 25(12) = 350$ dollars and Gym Q costs $20 + 35(12) = 440$ dollars, so Gym P is cheaper for a full year. Gym Q is cheaper only before month 3, because its monthly rate is higher. The 7 months comes from adding the join fees, $(50 + 20) \div 10$.$q$, 'draft', null)
